@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant showing the same PumpingStation as a SysML BDD vs a plain UML class diagram.
'   usecase:      Contrast «block» value/part/flow properties against plain UML attributes.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       methodology
' ============================================================================
title Example BDD - BDD vs UML Class

package "SysML Block Definition Diagram" {
  class "PumpingStation" <<block>> {
    flow in inletPressure : Pressure
    flow out outletFlow : FlowRate
    part pump : Pump
    part valve : Valve
    setpoint : Pressure
  }
  class "Pump" <<block>> {
    ratedFlow : FlowRate
  }
  class "Valve" <<block>> {
    aperture : Real
  }
  "PumpingStation" *-- "1" "Pump" : pump
  "PumpingStation" *-- "1" "Valve" : valve
}

package "Plain UML Class Diagram" {
  class "PumpingStationUML" as "PumpingStation" {
    inletPressure : double
    outletFlow : double
    pump : Pump
    valve : Valve
    setpoint : double
  }
  class "PumpUML" as "Pump" {
    ratedFlow : double
  }
  class "ValveUML" as "Valve" {
    aperture : double
  }
  "PumpingStation" *-- "1" "Pump"
  "PumpingStation" *-- "1" "Valve"
}

note bottom of "PumpingStation"
  SysML-specific property kinds NOT in UML class diagrams:
  - value property (typed by a valueType, e.g. setpoint : Pressure)
  - part property (composition of a block, role:pump)
  - flow property (in/out direction with item type, e.g. inletPressure : Pressure)
  UML collapses all of these into plain typed attributes.
end note

@enduml
